fix(members): stop showing a past workshop as "next workshop" on dashboard

The member dashboard (members/index.html) "Next event" card used
  .filter(e => e.dateObj >= now) ... [0] || eventsRes.data[0]
i.e. it explicitly fell back to eventsRes.data[0] when no event was in the
future. All events in the system were in the past (Jul 2, Jul 15), so the
fallback surfaced the July 15 "AI Structures" workshop as the "next workshop"
— directly contradicting the blog section that the same workshop already
happened (materials/quiz available) and there was nothing upcoming.

Now: only a genuinely future (or undated) event is shown as "next"; otherwise
the card reads "No upcoming workshops scheduled yet." Homepage ticker/timeline
were already correct (no fallback); only the member dashboard was affected.
